msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.machines.metainfo.xml:43
msgid "Follow what a running machine uses, and change its hardware"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.machines.metainfo.xml:47
msgid "Create a machine from an installation image"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.machines.metainfo.xml:53
msgid ""
"The details have a Passthrough group for Looking Glass, the memory balloon, "
"hiding the hypervisor from the guest, and the host's keyboard and mouse. "
"Looking Glass gets the SPICE listener and screen it needs, and is turned on "
"only where its client is installed. Advanced settings reach from the machine "
"type and power actions to disk and network card tuning, and the scripts "
"libvirt runs as a machine starts and stops can be edited, saved through an "
"administrator's password. The definition opens in a resizable editor with "
"XML highlighting, line numbers, and find and replace. A stopped machine "
"opens on its details and shows its screen once it starts, and a machine that "
"cannot start for want of huge pages says how many are missing."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.machines.metainfo.xml:54
msgid ""
"A disk or network card whose settings change at the next start is marked as "
"such, and a setting libvirt refuses shows as it was. Settings QEMU cannot "
"have, such as the host's system information on the user's own connection, "
"are no longer offered."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.machines.metainfo.xml:55
msgid ""
"The window no longer waits on libvirt as a connection or serial console "
"closes, as a screenshot is saved, or as the details look at the host's "
"devices and scripts. Usage graphs no longer take a sample from the machine "
"shown before, and the New Virtual Machine and Add Storage dialogs free their "
"memory once closed."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.machines.metainfo.xml:60
msgid ""
"A click in the console gives the virtual machine the shortcuts the desktop "
"would otherwise take, such as Super and Alt+Tab, until Ctrl+Alt releases the "
"keyboard, which the console says as it takes them. Fullscreen has a button "
"in the main window too, and in fullscreen the machine's controls, with the "
"keys to send, come down from the top edge of the screen: for a moment as "
"fullscreen starts, while the pointer is at the edge, and at a tap there on a "
"touch screen. The serial console says so while nothing has arrived from the "
"guest."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.machines.metainfo.xml:61
msgid ""
"A libvirt daemon that stops answering now shows as a lost connection instead "
"of leaving the window waiting. SPICE is offered only where QEMU has its "
"SPICE modules, and a machine that cannot start without them says what to "
"install. The console redraws only what changed of the guest's screen, and "
"screen readers know it by the machine's name."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.machines.metainfo.xml:66
msgid ""
"New virtual machines boot with the firmware chosen for them: BIOS, UEFI, or "
"UEFI with Secure Boot, which is the default where the host's firmware has "
"it, as Windows 11 requires. Their disk goes in the storage pool chosen for "
"it, which shows its free space, and their processors are cores of one "
"socket, so that Windows uses all of them."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.machines.metainfo.xml:67
msgid ""
"The serial console is offered only to machines with a serial port, which is "
"added and removed with the other devices. The sidebar selects a machine on a "
"click, no longer as the pointer passes over it. Fullscreen works from any "
"page, with F11 too, and going back to the list leaves it. The user session "
"explains why it has no virtual networks instead of failing to make one, and "
"a keyboard shortcuts dialog lists what the keyboard does."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.machines.metainfo.xml:71
msgid "First release."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.machines.policy:9
msgid "Change the scripts virtual machines run as they start and stop"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.machines.policy:10
msgid ""
"Authentication is required to change the scripts libvirt runs as root when a "
"virtual machine starts or stops"
msgstr ""

